{"slug":"hiero-json-rpc-relay","fork":"Blockchains/hiero-json-rpc-relay","upstream":"hiero-ledger/hiero-json-rpc-relay","branch":"main","commit":"874aeab52f227e650a683df981c23cbffab4be51","indexed_at":"2026-10-04T16:39:54Z","category":"hedera","description":"Implementation of Ethereum JSON-RPC APIs for Hedera","readme_summary":"Implementation of an Ethereum JSON RPC APIs for Hedera Hashgraph. Utilises both Hedera Consensus Nodes and Mirror nodes to support RPC queries as defined in the JSON RPC Specification - node (version 22) - npm - Docker (if you want to use `docker compose up` to run the server) We also recommend installing the \"prettier\" plugin in IntelliJ. There are two easy options to get your JSON RPC Relay up and running. You only need to do one of them. Spin up Docker containers (JSON RPC Relay source code & Redis Cache) 1. Run `npm install`. This will create populate and link `node_modules`. 2. Run `npm run build`. This will clean and compile the relay library and the server. 3. Disable Redis in .env by setting `REDIS_ENABLED=false`. This tells the JSON RPC Relay not to try and connect to Redis, which is likely not running on your computer. 4. Run `npm run start`. This will start the server on port ","install_commands":["git clone https://github.com/hiero-ledger/hiero-json-rpc-relay.git","docker compose up -d","npm run hopp","npm run acceptancetest","npm run bump-version --semver=0.21.0-rc1 --snapshot=true","docker build -t <owner>/hedera-json-rpc-relay .","docker tag <owner>/hedera-json-rpc-relay:latest ghcr.io/hiero-ledger/hiero-json-rpc-relay:main"],"languages_bytes":{"TypeScript":4461131,"Solidity":532868,"JavaScript":339089,"Go":44077,"Rust":6420,"Python":6260},"file_count":1133,"total_bytes":16904274,"licenses":[{"path":"LICENSE","detected":"Apache-2.0","head":"Apache License Version 2.0, January 2004 http://www.apache.org/licenses/ TERMS AND CONDITIONS FOR USE, REPRODUCTION, AND DISTRIBUTION 1. Definitions. \"License\" shall mean the terms and c